// Title: File Download via CertOC.EXE
// Sigma ID: 70ad0861-d1fe-491c-a45f-fa48148a300d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-05-16 | Modified: 2023-10-18
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects when a user downloads a file by using CertOC.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Certoc/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_certoc_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\certoc.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CertOC.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-GetCACAPS" and ProcessCommandLine contains "http")
